{#- The reviewer's report for one repo, in English. Context: see MarkdownReportWriter. -#}
# {{ repo.student.name }}{% if report.partner %} and {{ report.partner }}{% endif %}: {{ report.assignment_id }}

- Student: {{ repo.student.name }}
{% if report.partner %}
- Partner: {{ report.partner }}
{% endif %}
- Repo: {{ repo.url }}
- Commit: {{ short_sha or "not fetched" }}
{% if checked_commit %}
- Checked commit: {{ checked_commit }}
{% endif %}
- Run: {{ report.run_id }}
- Assignment: {{ report.assignment_id }}
- Status: {{ report.repo_run.status.value }}

## Build and run

{% if execution is none %}
The repo was not built or run.
{% else %}
- Target framework: {{ execution.target_framework or "not read" }}{% if execution.framework_outdated %} (older than the course's; the student is asked to move to it, and it never lowers the grade){% endif %}

- Prepare: {{ execution.prepare_status.value }}; build: {{ execution.build_status.value }}; run: {{ execution.run_status.value }}
{% if failure %}
- Failure: {{ failure }}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}

{% if assignments %}
## Assignments

{% for item in assignments %}
{% if item.reason_id == "assignment_not_applicable" %}
- {{ item.assignment_id }}: not checked: it does not apply to this repo ({{ item.detail }}).
{% elif item.reason_id == "assignment_condition_unknown" %}
- {{ item.assignment_id }}: not checked: whether it applies to this repo could not be decided ({{ item.detail }}). Review this repo first.
{% else %}
- {{ item.assignment_id }}: checked
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}

{% endif %}
{% if not sections and not not_evaluated and not report.repo_run.errors %}
Nothing to report: every checked requirement passed.
{% else %}
{% if sections %}
## Findings

{% for section in sections %}
### {{ section.label }} ({{ section.items | length }})

{% for item in section.items %}
- **{{ item.finding.requirement_id }}**: {{ item.title }}

  {{ item.finding.message_en | trim | indent(2) }}
{% if item.finding.evidence %}
{% set evidence = item.finding.evidence %}

  Evidence: `{{ evidence.file_path }}`, {% if evidence.line_start == evidence.line_end %}line {{ evidence.line_start }}{% else %}lines {{ evidence.line_start }}-{{ evidence.line_end }}{% endif %}:

  {{ evidence.quote | fence }}
  {{ evidence.quote | indent(2) }}
  {{ evidence.quote | fence }}
{% endif %}
{% for response in item.finding.responses %}

  The app answered {{ response.method.value }} {{ response.path }} with {{ response.status }}{% if response.body %} (the start of the response, the app's output):

  {{ response.body | fence }}
  {{ response.body | indent(2) }}
  {{ response.body | fence }}
{% else %} and an empty body.
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}

{% endfor %}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
{% if not_evaluated %}
## Not evaluated

{% for item in not_evaluated %}
{% if item.reason_id == "awaiting_reviewer" %}
- **{{ item.requirement_id }}**: {{ item.title }}. Checked by the code reviewer, which isn't enabled yet; never counted against the student.
{% elif item.reason_id == "windows_path" %}
- **{{ item.requirement_id }}**: {{ item.title }}. A request it needs answered with a server error after the app could not open {% for path in item.detail.split(", ") %}`{{ path }}`{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}: a path written with `\` as the folder separator, which works on Windows but not in the Linux container, so this was not held against the student. Check it by hand on Windows if needed.
{% elif item.reason_id == "dependency_failed" and item.detail %}
- **{{ item.requirement_id }}**: {{ item.title }}. It needs {{ item.detail }}, which failed, so it was not checked.
{% else %}
- **{{ item.requirement_id }}**: {{ item.title }}. {{ item.reason }}
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}

{% endif %}
{% if report.repo_run.errors %}
## Errors

{% for error in report.repo_run.errors %}
- {{ error }}
{% endfor %}

{% endif %}
{% endif %}
